  "description": "CIVJUQ crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H72 Ce6 N8 O48,4(C3 H7 N1 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1E (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1J (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2J (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1O (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.722-3.812 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.63-117.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6O4(OH)4(NO3)4(DMF)4(C8H5O3)8]·(DMF)4(H2O)2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
